                <pb facs="0676" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4001/20.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé to the
                            Acting Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter No. 605, of
                    yesterday’s date, which I at once forwarded to His Majesty’s principal secretary
                    of state for foreign affairs, I have the honor to communicate the following
                    telegram, which I have received this morning in reply from Sir Edward Grey:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Please express to Assistant Secretary of State my thanks for message. The
                            friendly attitude of the President and American Government is warmly
                            appreciated by His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esme Howard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
